From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:25:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: ACS: fall back to the BSS-based study

hostapd patch 889 (for upstream, hostap list), B138: with a 6 GHz
QCN9074 radio at 160 MHz and one channel per block in chanlist, ACS
failed and the radio stayed down whenever the radio had run on another
channel before (that channel keeps the only survey entry with a noise
floor; port 0035 rightly reports none for the others). Fall back to the
BSS-based study when the survey-based one finds no channel, and clear
the BSS-based mark at ACS cleanup.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile     |  2 +-
 ...based-study-when-the-survey-finds-no.patch | 67 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 68 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
index c14392e..ffaa096 100644
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=hostapd
-PKG_RELEASE:=12
+PKG_RELEASE:=13
 
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://w1.fi/hostap.git
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/889-ACS-fall-back-to-the-BSS-based-study-when-the-survey-finds-no.patch b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/889-ACS-fall-back-to-the-BSS-based-study-when-the-survey-finds-no.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8f1abe4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/889-ACS-fall-back-to-the-BSS-based-study-when-the-survey-finds-no.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+From c927563edeb439756e718b4011ee6058be9e5fe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:25:00 -0600
+Subject: [PATCH] ACS: Fall back to the BSS-based study when the survey finds no
+ channel
+
+acs_study() falls back to the BSS-based study only when no channel at
+all has sufficient survey data. When some do, but none that can be
+selected, ACS fails and the interface is not started. ath11k on
+QCN9074 reports a noise floor on 6 GHz only for a channel the radio
+operated on, so at 160 MHz with one channel per block in chanlist the
+radio failed to start after it had run on another channel.
+
+Run the BSS-based study in that case too, and clear its per-channel
+mark at ACS cleanup.
+
+Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/src/ap/acs.c
++++ b/src/ap/acs.c
+@@ -350,6 +350,7 @@ static void acs_cleanup_mode(struct host
+ 		chan->flag |= HOSTAPD_CHAN_SURVEY_LIST_INITIALIZED;
+ 		chan->min_nf = 0;
+ 		chan->punct_bitmap = 0;
++		chan->interference_bss_based = false;
+ 	}
+ }
+ 
+@@ -1316,6 +1317,21 @@ static int acs_study_options(struct host
+ }
+ 
+ 
++static bool acs_studied_bss_based(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
++{
++	int i;
++
++	if (!iface->current_mode)
++		return false;
++
++	for (i = 0; i < iface->current_mode->num_channels; i++)
++		if (iface->current_mode->channels[i].interference_bss_based)
++			return true;
++
++	return false;
++}
++
++
+ static void acs_study(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
+ {
+ 	struct hostapd_channel_data *ideal_chan;
+@@ -1328,6 +1344,16 @@ static void acs_study(struct hostapd_ifa
+ 	}
+ 
+ 	ideal_chan = acs_find_ideal_chan(iface);
++	if (!ideal_chan && !acs_studied_bss_based(iface)) {
++		/* The survey data was sufficient for some channels, but none
++		 * that could be selected, e.g., when the driver reports no
++		 * noise floor for the others. Use the BSS-based study, as
++		 * when no channel has sufficient survey data. */
++		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
++			   "ACS: Survey based ACS found no channel - trying BSS-based ACS");
++		if (acs_study_bss_based(iface) == 0)
++			ideal_chan = acs_find_ideal_chan(iface);
++	}
+ 	if (!ideal_chan) {
+ 		wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "ACS: Failed to compute ideal channel");
+ 		err = -1;
-- 
